  <accessrestrict id="3d32edb1a63511932c4a8aca5725a20b">
    <head>Conditions Governing Access</head>
<p>Open for research. When requesting to view audiovisual material, please refer to the Title and the AV Number (example: AV 1916). Researchers are asked to check the "Restrictions" note for each Title. If a Title does not currently have an access copy, please contact a RAC archivist for further instruction.</p>  </accessrestrict>
  <acqinfo id="aspace_6e2d9fd0e57a417dc5e40129c5fff316">
    <head>Immediate Source of Acquisition</head>
<p>In most cases, the specific details of the provenance are simply unknown.</p>  </acqinfo>
  <processinfo id="aspace_11ac589c56695f4bfea233e2c2f21fce">
    <head>Processing Information</head>
<p>Since the contents of the Film collection have inherently been separated from other archival holdings, the description of any individual item, or set of items, may also currently appear, in some form, in the finding aid for the originating collection.</p><p>Future processing, description, and presentation of Films will seek to address this issue as much as feasible.</p>  </processinfo>
  <scopecontent id="aspace_8d0ed83a30b4e46f1bace42763b79b76">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>The Audiovisual collection is an artificial collection created by the RAC to efficiently and effectively manage and present the moving images held among its archival holdings.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <separatedmaterial id="aspace_3560fdb771ece2d3c1d636f814e5f915">
    <head>Separated Materials</head>
<p>The majority of Audiovisual materials have been physically separated from a Rockefeller family archival collection.</p>  </separatedmaterial>
